{"id":11352,"date":"2024-05-05T10:31:49","date_gmt":"2024-05-05T17:31:49","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=11352"},"modified":"2024-06-03T13:50:00","modified_gmt":"2024-06-03T20:50:00","slug":"0-3-powering-charging-and-connecting","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-3-powering-charging-and-connecting\/","title":{"rendered":"0.3: Powering, charging, and connecting"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c653789\" name=\"6a2214c653789\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Powering on Zumi<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You can wake Zumi up by flipping the switch to the right towards the 1 position. In<br \/>\nprogramming, 1 means \u201cON\u201d or \u201cTRUE\u201d and 0 means \u201cOFF\u201d or \u201cFALSE.\u201d[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11498&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c6538a3\" name=\"6a2214c6538a3\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Powering off Zumi<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Although you can flip the switch to power off Zumi, it is best to properly shut down Zumi&#8217;s computer through the dashboard.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11682&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c653900\" name=\"6a2214c653900\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Low battery<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Zumi will beep and flash her lights when her battery is low. When this happens, you\u2019ll want to charge her battery.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11499&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<p class=\"p1\">You\u2019ll also be able to tell what her battery percentage is when she boots up by checking the screen. Later, you will learn how to find out the battery percentage from the dashboard.<\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11500&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c6539b4\" name=\"6a2214c6539b4\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Charging<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<strong>Charging when Zumi is OFF<\/strong><\/p>\n<p class=\"p1\">You can charge Zumi by plugging the micro USB cable into her micro USB port, located where you\u2019d usually find the gas tank on a car. You can plug the cable into an outlet adapter or to your computer\u2019s USB port.<\/p>\n<p>Zumi is fully charged when the red LED turns off. Then, you can disconnect the USB cable.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11501&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Charging when Zumi is ON<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Zumi can also be charged while she is on. This is very useful for when you\u2019re just coding and don\u2019t want to drain her battery.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11502&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]While charging, the red LED will be on. When Zumi is fully charged. the red LED will turn off.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11503&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]If you have broken the USB port, you can still charge Zumi using the Pi Zero Micro USB ports. Lift the side window to access the additional Micro USB ports.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11506&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c653a2c\" name=\"6a2214c653a2c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Connecting<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You are now ready to turn on Zumi and navigate to the dashboard. First, you need to learn about how you are connecting to Zumi. You will be connecting to Zumi <strong>wirelessly.\u00a0<\/strong>Imagine that Zumi will generate her own internet connection that you can connect to just like your home or school network.<\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11507&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]When you initially connect to Zumi, you will not be able to use the internet. That&#8217;s because you haven&#8217;t connected Zumi to the internet yet! If you don&#8217;t want to use the internet while connected to Zumi, you can skip connecting to the internet. Zumi is pre-loaded with lessons and is always shipped to you with the latest version of the dashboard.[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<strong>Connecting to the internet<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>If you connect Zumi to the internet, then you will be accessing your home or school network through Zumi. The video below will go over how to connect and check for updates.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11509&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>\u26a0\ufe0f Note:<\/strong> Zumi can only connect to 2.4 GHz WiFi networks, not 5 GHz networks. Most routers have both, but if yours doesn\u2019t, you may need to connect to a different network or use a mobile hotspot to update Zumi. Remember, connecting Zumi to a Wi-Fi network is <strong>optional.<\/strong>[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/iE-ILsVwj0k&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c653a76\" name=\"6a2214c653a76\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Next steps<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_single_image image=&#8221;11673&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Now, choose a programming language and start learning![\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 7 Powering on Zumi [vc_column_text]You can wake Zumi up by flipping the switch to the right towards the 1 position. In programming, 1 means \u201cON\u201d or \u201cTRUE\u201d and&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-3-powering-charging-and-connecting\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":2051,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":11339,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2135,2484,2177,2482,2483,2230],"class_list":["post-11352","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-connection","lesson-tag-getting-started","lesson-tag-internet","lesson-tag-updating","lesson-tag-zumi","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/11352","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":12,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/11352\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":11692,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/11352\/revisions\/11692"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/2051"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=11352"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=11352"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=11352"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}